<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sima Xin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/203-bce">203 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sima Xin was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> officer who surrendered with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-han">Zhang Han</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiang-yu">Xiang Yu</a> in 207 BCE. In 206 BCE Xiang Yu made him King of Sai, one of the three kingdoms carved from the Qin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-bang">Liu Bang</a> conquered Sai the same year; Sima Xin later rejoined Xiang Yu and killed himself after a defeat at Chenggao in 203 BCE.</p></div>
